{"name":"Red Damask","hex":"#cb6f4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"damask","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ornate silk fabric originating from Damascus.","Linen so woven that a pattern is produced by the different directions of the thread, without contrast of colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a grayish-pink colour, like that of the damask rose."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damask"}],"entries":[{"title":"Damask","blocks":[{"text":"Damask is a woven, reversible patterned fabric. Damasks are woven by periodically reversing the action of the warp and weft threads. The pattern is most commonly created with a warp-faced satin weave and the ground with a weft-faced or sateen weave."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/ItalianSilkDamask.jpg/330px-ItalianSilkDamask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Damask"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Damask_with_floral_sprigs%2C_Italy%2C_Baroque%2C_1600-1650%2C_silk_two-tone_damask_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC04376.JPG/500px-Damask_with_floral_sprigs%2C_Italy%2C_Baroque%2C_1600-1650%2C_silk_two-tone_damask_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC04376.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Damask_with_floral_sprigs%2C_Italy%2C_Baroque%2C_1600-1650%2C_silk_two-tone_damask_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC04376.JPG/1280px-Damask_with_floral_sprigs%2C_Italy%2C_Baroque%2C_1600-1650%2C_silk_two-tone_damask_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC04376.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Damask_with_floral_sprigs%2C_Italy%2C_Baroque%2C_1600-1650%2C_silk_two-tone_damask_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC04376.JPG/500px-Damask_with_floral_sprigs%2C_Italy%2C_Baroque%2C_1600-1650%2C_silk_two-tone_damask_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC04376.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Damask with floral sprigs, Italy, Baroque, 1600–1650, silk two-tone damask","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADamask_with_floral_sprigs%2C_Italy%2C_Baroque%2C_1600-1650%2C_silk_two-tone_damask_-_Royal_Ontario_Museum_-_DSC04376.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Woman%27s_Spitalfields_silk_damask_shoes_with_buckles_1740s.jpg/500px-Woman%27s_Spitalfields_silk_damask_shoes_with_buckles_1740s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th